comments.body:
@ironbelly thank you for writing this up. A read-through of the approval flow found the same shared-login point, and we would like to add a view. Please correct anything we have misread.

We read the shared login as a lower priority than the other watcher and coordinator work for now. The approval still needs a person to decide, and in practice the person tells an agent in chat and the agent sets the field. What would help is a recorded decision, even if it is "accepted for now, revisit when more people use one workspace", so the code's warning-only check (and the assignee rule in #698) stops being an open question. Would you be willing to record that, or does the owner prefer one of the four options in this issue first?

Happy to help with either.
